WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.829 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  fbi agents removed around 20 boxes of  items during their search at former  president donald trump's mar-a-lago home  on august 8th according to a search  warrant released by a florida court  friday investigators recovered 11 sets  of classified information including some  that was so top secret it is designated  to be only open in a secure government  location a list of items removed from  the property reference one set of  documents marked as various classified  slash ts  sci documents an abbreviation that  refers to top secret sensitive  compartmented information it also says  agents collected four sets of top secret  documents three sets of secret documents  and three sets of confidential documents  the list didn't provide any more details  about the substance of the files  top secret documents could include  anything from military secrets defense  secrets  information that would be pertinent to  our national security interests the list  is contained in a seven-page document  that also includes the warrant to search  the premises which was granted by a  federal magistrate judge in florida  the warrant shows that fbi agents sought  to search the quote 45 office as well as  all storage rooms and other rooms used  by the former president  they didn't seek access to private guest  rooms such as those of mar-a-lago  members according to the document  attorney general merrick garland said  thursday that he approved the decision  to seek the search warrant and called  for its release  the department filed the motion  to make public the warrant and receipt  in light of the former president's  public confirmation of the search  the surrounding circumstances and the  substantial public interest in this  matter he sort of in some ways was  putting the burden on trump to say no  don't release this but instead we saw  the president say that he had no problem  with releasing it and that he feels that  this entire thing is a politically  motivated witch hunt in a post on his  social media platform thursday trump  said his representatives had been  cooperating fully and that the  government could have had whatever they  wanted if we had it trump's lawyers  argue that the former president used his  authority to declassify the material  before he left office while a president  has the power to declassify documents a  sitting president has that power there  are federal regulations laying out that  process for doing so  it is unclear how the investigation may  progress and whether prosecutors are  considering bringing any charges against  trump this is just a first little  glimpse into what is probably a  sprawling investigation into the former  president's handling of classified  material

